#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# some

#% text
# `some(xs, p)` gives `true` when `p(x)` is `true` for at least one element `x` of `xs`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
some([1, 3, 4], is_even)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
some([1, 3, 5], is_even)
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# An empty list has no element that passes:

#% cell
some([], is_even)
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `every`, `any_true`, `select`
